    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d785">

                <pb facs="0719" n="635" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg635"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/2988</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-10-29T12:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1917, 12
                        noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5677. The following, strictly confidential, received from Copenhagen today:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of telegram No. 1482 of October 25, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra.</hi>]</p>
                <p>Please take up matter with Minister of Foreign Affairs orally and ascertain his
                    views. Also what steps, if any, British Government contemplates taking. Similar
                    instructions telegraphed Ambassador at Paris.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d785-f1"/>
                    Text furnished Petrograd<anchor n="3" xml:id="d785-f2"/> to report as to
                    authenticity without making any representations whatever.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
